From 280718ee97525fe46d469f0ff130451ebdff8678 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:45:37 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 109/109] Ad hoc: ask how to play over the game when nothing is
 chosen

With a public server (patch 0108), a player who goes online with
nothing chosen is asked how to play, on screens over the paused game,
instead of the game failing to find a server.

- ui/choice_screen: choose_over_game, notice_over_game and
  type_over_game, screens over the paused game (no input to the game,
  its sound stopped, the skin's sounds muted so none plays late), one
  pause for screens opened from one another; PortableKit's own look when
  a port has no skin.
- DialogSkin::choices (ChoiceSkinView: a title, a prompt, items with a
  detail each) for a port to draw them in its game's look; a keyboard can
  ask for that look too (TextInputRequest::game_look).
- ui/adhoc_chooser: Online ("How do you want to play?"): Play Online with
  the players on now (dimmed, with the reason, while the server's address
  is not known), Host a Session, Join a Session, Back. Join lists the
  sessions on this network, recent addresses and Enter an Address (the
  keyboard), Back. Host starts hosting and says what the router answered
  (the internet address, copied), or why players on the internet cannot
  reach this PC.
- adhoc_ask_for_choice(), set by the interface (set_adhoc_chooser): from
  sceNetAdhocctlInit, and again when a room, a Discover search or a
  Netconf connection still finds nothing chosen. False only when the
  player was asked and backed out. <prefix>_NO_ADHOC_CHOOSER=1 turns it
  off.
- GameProfile::adhoc_choice_at_init: a port that asks from its game's
  menu turns the sceNetAdhocctlInit question off. By then a game is
  usually on its way to an online screen, and Back cannot return to the
  menu the player came from.
- The keyboard: back with nothing typed cancels, as Cancel does, on a new
  press (held down to delete, it stops at the empty field); the hint says
  Back then instead of Delete.

Tested with Dissidia 012's port on Windows (clang), its own look, one and
two copies with the server on loopback: the chooser asked from the
port's menu; Join by typed address; Play Online with the count, chosen
and remembered, both copies meeting in a lobby; Host and its notice; Back
from every screen and the keyboard's back. The framework tests pass but
for portablekit_settings_tests, which does not link on this branch: its
target lacks the controller picker's player-device functions, and no
file of this change is involved. The ad hoc tests were not run
(firewall). Not tested: the
router's notices, PortableKit's own look, touch, a mouse, Linux, Android,
another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
